# Cleanup temporary artifacts

When the task is done (or abandoned), remove one-off files created only for investigation, DB probing, E2E harnesses, screenshots, Playwright installs, or local run logs.

## Do delete after the task
- Ad-hoc `scripts/` helpers (Python/JS/PS1), `_scratch/`, `.agent-tmp/`, `tmp-agent/`
- `*-run.log`, `fe-run.log`, `be-run.log`, `be-test-run.log`
- Local `ui-shots/`, `node_modules` under scratch folders, PNG captures from probes
- Password-reset / credential probe scripts

## Do keep (commit when the user asks)
- Real product code under `src/`
- Intentional migrations/seeds under `src/main/resources/db/migration/`
- Intentional tracked scripts already in the repo (e.g. backend `scripts/postgres/`, `scripts/load_test_tenant.sh`)
- `.gitignore` and Cursor rules that prevent reintroducing junk

## Practice
1. Prefer putting throwaway work under ignored paths (`/scripts/`, `/_scratch/`) when a temporary file is unavoidable.
2. Before saying a task is complete, delete those throwaways so `git status` shows only meaningful source changes.
3. Never leave hundreds of generated files (e.g. Playwright `node_modules`) for the user to triage before push.
4. Do not commit secrets, connection passwords, or reset-password utilities.
